     Well, I could come back with the old line about strategy and skill,
but I think it's more applicable that the non-agressive moves should be
for *movement* only.  Not waiting.  It shouldn't wait when you moves
into your pet, and it shouldn't wait when you move into a monster
either.  (Of course, I still like the move-pet option that Hairston
brought up, but that's a different matter.  Unless you want to debate
whether it should be a non-agressive or agressive move.)
     So I don't like putting in a "free swipe."  Especially since there
would no longer be any continuous movement command when the number-pad
is in use: ctrl-<dir> doesn't register due to some brain damage in the
key --> extended ASCII code routine.  Or, rather, it does, except for the
up and down arrows, and it's not implemented in the MS-DOS version (and
couldn't be, without fiddling with the interrupt controller).  G-<dir>
would still work, I grant.
     Just to note, for convenience, I think a non-agressive move into a
monster should take no time and instead indicate its state: hostile,
peaceful or tame.  "The black dragon is hungry."  :)

